course: dictionary
lesson: 12568
title: Diligence: steady, careful work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diligence is a noun. It means careful, steady hard work that keeps going until the job is done properly. Clues in the sentence help: «Mia checked her sums three times, and her diligence meant she made almost no mistakes.» Checking three times is careful work, so diligence must mean care and effort.
explain: The word comes from diligent (an adjective) and diligently (an adverb). «Ben is a diligent gardener who weeds the beds every Saturday.» «Lily studied diligently for her test.» All three words come from the same idea of steady, careful effort.
explain: Schools use diligence to praise effort and not giving up. Teachers often write it on reports and posters. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Her diligence paid off when she finally won the art prize.» Does "her careful, steady hard work paid off" make sense? It does, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Diligence means careful, steady hard work that keeps going until the job is done properly.
fact: Diligent is the adjective (a diligent student) and diligently is the adverb (she worked diligently).
fact: Due diligence means checking something carefully before a big decision, such as buying a company or a house.
fact: Long ago, a diligence was also a stagecoach in France and nearby countries.
fact: Phrases to learn: «with diligence», «due diligence», and «hard work and diligence».
exercise: «Mia checked her sums three times. Her diligence meant she made almost no mistakes.» What does diligence mean? | Sitting still and doing nothing | Shouting answers out loud | *Careful, steady hard work | Quick guessing without checking
exercise: «Ben is a diligent gardener who weeds the beds every Saturday.» Find and copy the one word that means hard-working and careful. | Saturday | Ben | *diligent | gardener
exercise: «Lily studied diligently for her test.» What does diligently mean here? | *With careful, steady effort | Loudly, with the radio on | Carelessly and in a rush | Only once in a while
test: «Before he bought the old house, Dad did due diligence and paid an expert to check it.» What does due diligence mean here? | *Checking something carefully before a big decision | Dancing around the house | Painting every room | Selling the house quickly
test: «Tom showed great ___ in his reading all year.» Which word fits the gap best? | Boredom | Silliness | Laziness | *Diligence
exam: Which sentence uses diligence correctly? | The rain had great diligence and fell all afternoon. | The team lost interest and stopped trying, which showed great diligence. | *She showed diligence by checking her project carefully over many days. | He ate his lunch with diligence in under a minute.
